course: dictionary
lesson: 15165
title: Reading angry faces
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Scowling means making an angry, cross face, with your eyebrows pulled down low and your mouth turned down.
explain: Writers use scowling to show feelings without telling you directly. «Mum was scowling at the muddy boots on the clean carpet.» You know she is cross because of her face, even though the sentence never says "angry".
explain: Scowling can be a verb, something a person does: «The giant scowled.» It can also be an adjective, describing a noun: «a scowling giant» is a giant who looks angry.
fact: Scowl is the root word. Scowling is the -ing form, and scowled is the past tense.
fact: «Scowling» often comes with «at»: «scowling at» someone means frowning angrily at them.
fact: «A scowling face» means a face that looks cross or angry.
fact: A scowl shows feelings through the face, so writers use it to show how a character feels.
fact: «Scowled» can describe the past: «Dad scowled at the late bus.»
exercise: «The bus driver was scowling at the late runners.» What is the driver feeling? | Very sleepy | Happy and excited | Lost in thought | *Cross and angry
exercise: In «a scowling giant», what kind of word is scowling? | A verb showing the giant ran | *An adjective describing the giant | A noun for a place | A name
exercise: Which word means making an angry face? | *Scowling | Yawning | Smiling | Giggling
test: «The cat sat scowling at the dog.» What does the cat look like? | Pleased and calm | Hungry for dinner | Sleepy and tired | *Cross and grumpy
test: «The scowling teacher pointed at the door.» What does scowling tell you about the teacher? | She is asleep | She is laughing at a joke | *She is angry | She is lost
exam: Which sentence shows a character scowling at someone? | *Grandma scowled at the muddy footprints | The girl laughed at the joke | The boy yawned in class | The dog wagged its tail
